cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book, please cite it as below."
type: book
title: "Implementing AI in Academic Medicine: A guide to governance and principled practice"
# NOTE: family-names and given-names were transposed in every release through
# 2026-04-27 ("family-names: Sean, given-names: Davis"), so citation managers
# rendered the author as "Sean, D." Corrected 2026-08-07.
authors:
  - family-names: "Davis"
    given-names: "Sean"
    email: seandavi@gmail.com
    affiliation: "University of Colorado Anschutz School of Medicine"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8991-6458"
abstract: >-
  A governance framework for academic medical centers deploying AI across
  clinical care, research, education, and business operations. The book treats
  an AMC as four semi-independent AI domains rather than one, connected by five
  cross-cutting workstreams — data access, infrastructure and security, ethics
  and regulation, workforce capacity, and lifecycle management — and the
  steering function that ties them together.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - governance
  - academic medical center
  - clinical AI
  - research AI
  - medical education
  - health policy
  - regulation
  - ethics
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://seandavi.github.io/amc-ai-governance/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/seandavi/amc-ai-governance"
version: "2026-08-07"
date-released: "2026-08-07"
# Concept DOI (…585) — always resolves to the latest release.
# NOT …586, which is the *version* DOI for the 2026-04-27 release. That version
# DOI was in this file and on the README badge until 2026-08-07, which pinned
# every citation to a frozen pre-audit version of the book.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.19820585"
